schema: claim-evidence
object:
  title: ERC-20 (introduced 2015) remains the foundation for most token-based systems
  type: claim-evidence
  claim: >-
    The ERC-20 standard for fungible tokens was introduced in 2015 on the
    Ethereum blockchain and remains the foundation for most token-based
    systems today.
  evidence: >-
    General assertion, sourced generically to ethereum.org in the article's
    references; no specific ERC-20 proposal document (EIP-20) or adoption
    statistic is cited.
  source_lineage: src/content/docs/what-are-tokens.md
  interpretation: >-
    Used to anchor the token-standards section, giving a concrete historical
    date to an otherwise conceptual explanation of fungible-token mechanics.
  uncertainty: >-
    "Remains the foundation for most token-based systems" is a broad,
    unquantified claim; no adoption data (e.g., number of live ERC-20
    contracts) is cited to support "most."
  maturity: raw
  public_use: source-linked-unreviewed
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/what-are-tokens.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
